          "segment_index": 12,
          "source_segment_id": "seg-9c11e3e5c943b04fe92b68d3",
          "source_text_sha256": "1c9698398babd6bfd7ab067c57cba9ca428803db4dff7d75b5c0daa6dc8058b9",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On October 13, 2013, four pilots (see the estimated positions of the 4 aircraft on the aeronautical questionnaire) observed a powerful light phenomenon in the east of France, a phenomenon also observed on the ground (see press article), and by the Chaligny camera (near Nancy) of the BOAM network. This phenomenon, called a bolide, was characterized as an atmospheric reentry of a meteoroid (meteorite fall). The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"A\".",
